/**
\page tiff_processing_pipeline TIFF image processing pipeline

\tableofcontents

\section tiff_pipeline_scope Inspection and transformation

The TIFF tools share `CTiffImg` and libtiff, but have different output
contracts. The diagram separates metadata inspection from the two single-IFD
transform paths. All directory indexes below refer to the zero-based main IFD
chain. SubIFDs are a separate graph and are not selected by `--ifd`.

\dotfile tiff-pipeline.dot "TIFF inspection and single-IFD transformation paths"

| Tool | Input choice | Pixel processing | Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| \ref profiles_lane "iccApplyProfiles" | Main IFD 0 by default; `--ifd N` overrides JSON `imageFiles.srcIfd` | Decode selected image, apply forward or inverse-search profile chain | One transformed TIFF IFD |
| \ref specsep_lane "iccSpecSepToTiff" | Same `--ifd N` main-chain index in every numbered grayscale input | Decode selected input bands and combine channels | One spectral TIFF IFD |
| \ref tiffdump_lane "iccTiffDump" | `--ifd N` for one IFD, or `--list-directories` for main-chain inventory | Metadata only; no pixel decode | Human/JSON inspection, optional embedded ICC extraction |

Both transforms warn when additional main IFDs or selected-directory SubIFD
references are present. They do not copy those directories. TiffDump lists
SubIFD offsets without following them; its successful inspection does not
validate the image pixels.

\section tiff_pipeline_bounds Decode and inventory bounds

The main-chain inventory is bounded at 4096 directories. The default decoded
strip or tile-band buffer limit is 256 MiB. `ICCDEV_TIFF_MAX_DECODE_MIB`
allows an explicit higher per-buffer limit for trusted inputs; it does not
bound total process memory, file size, pixel count, IFD metadata, or embedded
profile size. SpecSep also accounts for concurrently open input tile bands
against an aggregate budget. Tiled and BigTIFF output are explicit choices;
otherwise output is classic stripped TIFF.

\section tiff_pipeline_receipts Version and QA evidence

Each TIFF tool's help and `--version` output identifies its IccProfLib build
version and linked libtiff runtime version. ApplyProfiles also reports its
IccLibConnect build version. When compiled with
`ICCDEV_ENABLE_TELEMETRY=ON`, ApplyProfiles records the selected IFD, its
default/JSON/CLI provenance, and inventory counts. SpecSep records default
versus explicit selection and aggregate input counts. TiffDump records the
selected directory in single-IFD mode, or visited counts when listing the
main chain. See \ref md_docs_2iccapply_2apply-profile-processing
"ApplyProfiles processing QA" for the output validation contract.

\section tiff_pipeline_followup Known follow-up work

The current transform writers open the final destination path before all
decoding completes. A late failure can truncate or remove a pre-existing
destination. A staged-output change and its failure regressions are described
in \ref md_docs_2analysis_2image-tool-tiff-qa-2026-11-01
"the image-tool audit and implementation plan". Use a fresh destination for
current QA runs.
*/
